2. Spread Operator
The spread operator (...) is used to expand or copy elements from an array or properties from an object.
Array
const numbers1 = [10, 20, 30];

const numbers2 = [...numbers1];

console.log(numbers2);
Output:
[10, 20, 30]
Combine arrays
const first = [10, 20];
const second = [30, 40];

const result = [...first, ...second];

console.log(result);
Output:
[10, 20, 30, 40]
Add new elements
const numbers = [20, 30];

const result = [10, ...numbers, 40];

console.log(result);
Output:
[10, 20, 30, 40]

Object Spread
const student = {
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 22
};

const updatedStudent = {
    ...student,
    city: "Pune"
};

console.log(updatedStudent);
Output:
{
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 22,
    city: "Pune"
}
Updating an object
const student = {
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 22
};

const updatedStudent = {
    ...student,
    age: 23
};

console.log(updatedStudent);
